; A map whose members all load, link and check, and whose only defect is a
; DECLARED ALIGNMENT THAT DOES NOT HOLD: the two claims are exact opposites, so
; asserting they are `same` is false. This is the negative anchor whose parity
; is observable, because the envelope IS derivable — the failure happens after
; the checked boundary, so both drivers are handed the same bytes and must both
; refuse them at exit 1 with nothing on stdout.
;
; The members are the agreement fixture's, named through a parent-relative path
; rather than copied, which also exercises path resolution against the
; MANIFEST's own directory rather than the process working directory.
(lara-map@1
  (policy empirical-v1 ../agreement/empirical-v1.policy.lara)
  (backends (backend nd 1))
  (members
    (member paper_pos ../agreement/pos.lara)
    (member paper_neg ../agreement/neg.lara))
  (alignments
    (alignment
      (ref paper_pos c_pos whole)
      (ref paper_neg c_neg whole)
      same
      (author reviewer_r)
      (audit-status disputed)
      (rationale "Deliberately false: improves(M, accuracy, D) is not not_improves(M, accuracy, D).")))
  (questions))
